1
00:00:00,705 --> 00:00:03,548
One profile write is waiting for a file lock.

2
00:00:03,548 --> 00:00:05,760
Other requests should keep moving.

3
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:10,057
We ask the heartbeat endpoint a very small question: are you alive?

4
00:01:21,698 --> 00:01:24,395
The answer arrives after the lock timeout.

5
00:01:24,395 --> 00:01:28,632
It is technically alive, and approximately one coffee break late.

6
00:01:28,632 --> 00:01:33,447
A profile-store wait has paused unrelated requests on the same event loop.

7
00:01:34,441 --> 00:01:38,732
This high severity service stall was confirmed twice in fresh servers.

8
00:01:38,732 --> 00:01:44,554
Idle heartbeats stayed below one second; contended heartbeats took about twenty eight seconds.
